%I A401399 #12 Oct 29 2026 00:11:42
%S A401399 1,2,4,4,5,14,6,6,7,14,8,12,7,8,8,9,9,8,9
%N A401399 Least k such that a majority of free k-celled polyominoes contain a copy of the free polyomino with binary code A246521(n).
%C A401399 Least k such that A401398(n,k) < A000105(k)/2.
%C A401399 Can be read as an irregular triangle, whose n-th row contains A000105(n) terms, n >= 1.
%e A401399 As an irregular triangle:
%e A401399    1;
%e A401399    2;
%e A401399    4,  4;
%e A401399    5, 14,  6, 6, 7;
%e A401399   14,  8, 12, 7, 8, 8, 9, 9, 8, 9, ?, 11
%e A401399 For n = 7, the polyomino with binary code A246521(7) = 23 is the square tetromino. The number of free k-celled polyominoes that do not contain a copy of the square tetromino is A401398(7,k) = A401400(k). For k < 14, A401400(k) >= A000105(k)/2, but A401400(14) = 421856 < A000105(14)/2 = 901971/2, so a(7) = 14.
%Y A401399 Cf. A000105, A246521, A401398, A401400.
%K A401399 nonn,tabf,more,new
%O A401399 2,2
%A A401399 _Pontus von Brömssen_, Oct 24 2026
